{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BringLatticeSpan","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BringLatticeSpan","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Determinant","lean:module:QOU.BringConeSplitChirality"],"declarations":24,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.bring_realisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.bring_realisation","kind":"theorem","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L347-L373","doc":"**The hypotheses are not vacuous.** Over `ℝ`, with `φ = 2cos(π/5)` and `r = 2cos(π/4)`,\nthe elements `s = i` and `u = φ/2 − (r/2)·i + (√(φ−1)/2)·j` satisfy every hypothesis of\n`bring_span_eq_top`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.bring_left_mul_scalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.bring_left_mul_scalar","kind":"theorem","line":329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L329-L343","doc":"**`commutes_span_scalar` with its spanning hypothesis discharged.** Under the hypotheses\nof `bring_span_eq_top`, a left multiplication `L_v` that commutes with every element of\n`S` is a scalar. So on a quotient by such an `S`, the second complex structure of the Hopf\nmodel does not descend. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.bring_span_eq_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.bring_span_eq_top","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L307-L327","doc":"**Bring's triangle group spans.** Let `s, u` be as in `bring_relations`, with `φ, r > 0`.\nLet `S` be multiplicatively closed and contain some positive power of every element of\nthe monoid generated by `s` and `u`. That holds when `S` is a finite-index normal subgroup,\nsuch as the lift of Bring's `Γ₄`, by Mathlib `Subgroup.pow_index_mem`. Then `S` spans\n`M₂(R)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.bring_x_y","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.bring_x_y","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L272-L305","doc":"**Two hyperbolic elements of the triangle group with a non-degenerate commutator.**\n`x = s·u²` and `y = u²·s` have `N = 1`, `T = φr > 2`, `T(xy) = φ` and\n`N(xy − yx) = 1 − φ ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.bring_relations","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.bring_relations","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L246-L270","doc":"**The trace data force the `(2,5,4)` relations**: `s² = −1`, `u⁵ = −1`, `(su)⁴ = −1`,\ni.e. `X² = Y⁵ = (XY)⁴ = 1` in `PSL(2)`. Generic `[CommRing K]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.span_eq_top_of_hyperbolic_powers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.span_eq_top_of_hyperbolic_powers","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L219-L232","doc":"**Positive powers of two hyperbolic elements with a non-degenerate commutator span.**\nLet `x, y` have `N = 1`, `T > 2`, and `N(xy − yx) ≠ 0`. If a submonoid `S` contains some\npositive power of `x` and some positive power of `y`, then `S` spans `M₂(R)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.seqB_succ_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.seqB_succ_pos","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L214-L217","doc":"`b_{n+1} > 0` for a hyperbolic trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.seqB_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.seqB_mono","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L201-L212","doc":"For a hyperbolic trace `T > 2` with `N = 1`, the sequence is nonnegative and strictly\nincreasing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.pow_succ_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.pow_succ_eq","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L182-L193","doc":"**Powers.** `x^(n+1) = −N(x)·bₙ + b_{n+1}·x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.seqB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.seqB","kind":"def","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L176-L180","doc":"The coefficient sequence of powers: `b₀ = 0`, `b₁ = 1`, `b_{n+2} = T·b_{n+1} − N·bₙ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.comm_affine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.comm_affine","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L169-L174","doc":"`[α + βx, γ + δy] = βδ·[x, y]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.span_submonoid_eq_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.span_submonoid_eq_top","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L155-L167","doc":"A submonoid containing `x, y` with `N(xy − yx)` a unit spans `M₂(R)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.span_eq_top_of_isUnit_rnorm_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.span_eq_top_of_isUnit_rnorm_comm","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L145-L153","doc":"**Spanning criterion.** If `N(xy − yx)` is a unit, then `1, x, y, xy` span `M₂(R)` (and\nare a basis). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.det_one_x_y_xy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.det_one_x_y_xy","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L132-L143","doc":"**The determinant of `1, x, y, xy` is `−N(xy − yx)/4`.** In the basis `1, i, j, k`, the\ndeterminant of the four vectors `1, x, y, xy`, times `−4`, is the reduced norm of the\nadditive commutator. This is an exact identity in any commutative ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.rnorm_comm_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.rnorm_comm_eq","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L121-L130","doc":"**Fricke identity** for the split quaternions. On `SL₂` (`N = 1`) the right-hand side is\n`2 − tr(xyx⁻¹y⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.rtr_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.rtr_conj","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L114-L119","doc":"`T(a·B·a) = T(a)·T(Ba) − N(a)·T(B)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.rtr_mul_mul_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.rtr_mul_mul_self","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L107-L112","doc":"`T(a·b²) = T(b)·T(ab) − N(b)·T(a)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.rtr_mul_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.rtr_mul_self","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L101-L105","doc":"`T(x²) = T(x)² − 2N(x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.rtr_mul_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.rtr_mul_comm","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L96-L99","doc":"The reduced trace is cyclic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.mul_self_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.mul_self_eq","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L91-L94","doc":"**Cayley–Hamilton**: `x² = T(x)·x − N(x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.rnorm_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.rnorm_smul","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L86-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.rnorm_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.rnorm_mul","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L81-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.rtr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.rtr","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L78-L79","doc":"The reduced trace (`= tr` under `M₂(R)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.rnorm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.rnorm","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringLatticeSpan.lean#L74-L76","doc":"The reduced norm of the split quaternions (`= det` under `M₂(R)`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}